The fields of a query's <Name>Params and <Name>Row types must be unique too: output
columns views_1 and views1 both become the field Views1 of PageDaysRow, and parameters
page_1 and page1 both become the field Page1 of PageDaysParams. Each diagnostic points at
the later name.
-- dynaflux/page_views.sql --
CREATE STREAM page_views (
    user_id String,
    page    String
)
PRIMARY KEY (user_id);
-- dynaflux/page_daily.sql --
CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW page_daily
ORDER BY (page, day)
PRIMARY KEY (page)
AS SELECT
    page,
    toDate(event_time) AS day,
    count()            AS views
FROM page_views
GROUP BY page, day;
-- dynaflux/queries.sql --
-- name: PageDays :many
SELECT day, views AS views_1, views AS views1
FROM page_daily
WHERE page IN ({page_1:String}, {page1:String});
-- want --
dynaflux/queries.sql:2:40: error DF1207
dynaflux/queries.sql:4:33: error DF1207
-- want-text --
dynaflux/queries.sql:2:40: error DF1207: PageDays: generated Go name Views1 for the field of column views1 of query PageDays collides with the field of column views_1 of query PageDays at dynaflux/queries.sql:2
  hint: rename one of them, or set -- go:type on the stream
dynaflux/queries.sql:4:33: error DF1207: PageDays: generated Go name Page1 for the field of parameter page1 of query PageDays collides with the field of parameter page_1 of query PageDays at dynaflux/queries.sql:4
  hint: rename one of them, or set -- go:type on the stream
